Lab 12: Managing Configuration and Sensitive Data with ConfigMaps and Secrets


1. ConfigMap ivolvecm (non-sensitive config)
bash 
kubectl create configmap ivolvecm --from-literal=DB_USER=ivolve-user --from-literal=DB_HOST=db --dry-run=client -o yaml  > configmap.yml

configmap.yml:
yaml
apiVersion: v1
data:
  DB_HOST: db
  DB_USER: ivolve-user
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: ivolvecm
      
bash
kubectl apply -f configmap.yml


2. Secret ivolvesecret (sensitive credentials, Base64-encoded)

Encode the values first. Use -n, otherwise a newline becomes part of the password:

bash
echo -n 'RootPass@123' | base64      # Um9vdFBhc3NAMTIz
echo -n 'UserPass@123' | base64      # VXNlclBhc3NAMTIz
Then create Secrets 
secerts.yml:
yaml

apiVersion: v1
data:
  DB_PASSWORD: YVhadmJIWmxMWFZ6WlhJSw==
  MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: YVhadmJIWmxNVEl6Q2c9PQ==
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: ivolvesecret

bash
kubectl apply -f secerts.yml
3. Verify
bash
kubectl get configmap ivolvecm -n ivolve -o yaml
kubectl describe configmap ivolvecm -n ivolve

kubectl get secret ivolvesecret -n ivolve
kubectl describe secret ivolvesecret -n ivolve        # shows sizes only, not values


